{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And I heard.</b> He is speaking to the seraphim; therefore the word לנו ['for us']." "And the meaning of <b>Here am I, send me</b>: after his lips were purified, he is fit to be a messenger — and he was not so previously. Therefore I said that from this passage begins the prophecy of Isaiah."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:23.786909172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}